  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run the app, so the physics and the rendering are untested. The scene is a concrete yard with the 15-crate pyramid (5,4,3,2,1 rows) on the left. A lattice crane with a 6-unit chain and steel ball stands on the right.\n\n- **Rendering:** it uses `@aura3d/engine` with a procedural Preetham sky, a neutral environment and a shadowed key light. Nothing is loaded from the network. I didn't use `looks.preset`, because its HDRI would be a fetch.\n- **Physics:** the engine's physics wasn't suited to a pendulum plus a stacked pyramid, so I wrote my own at a fixed 1/240 s step. Crates are cubes with collision, friction (0.5 against each other, 0.7 on the ground) and restitution. The ball is a 40-mass sphere held at a fixed rope length from the pivot.\n- **Stability:** the whole pyramid sleeps until the ball touches it, so it stands still before the swing. I haven't checked how stable it is once awake.\n- **Controls:** \"Swing\" pulls the ball back to +60° over about 1.1 s and releases it. The ball is on the right (+x) and the pyramid on the left, so the angle starts at +60 and passes through 0. \"Reset\" rebuilds the stack and returns the ball to rest. Both are DOM buttons overlaid on the canvas.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only getter, updated every frame. `displaced` counts crates whose centre has moved more than 0.75 units from its start. The phase becomes `'settled'` once the ball has hit, the crates are asleep and the ball is nearly still. If that doesn't happen, it settles after 14 s.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\nCamera framing, shadow coverage, whether the swing scatters the crates as intended, and whether the pyramid stays up when awake all need a look in a browser.",
